1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:03,293
MyCampusView Academy.

2
00:00:03,343 --> 00:00:06,166
Robotics 101, video 9.

3
00:00:06,216 --> 00:00:09,170
Reading the IR sensors.

4
00:00:10,350 --> 00:00:14,305
Before the robot can follow a line, we must be sure it

5
00:00:14,355 --> 00:00:15,565
can see the line.

6
00:00:15,615 --> 00:00:20,460
In this video, you will read both sensors and print what they see.

7
00:00:21,850 --> 00:00:24,685
First we give the pins names.

8
00:00:24,735 --> 00:00:28,564
LEFT_IR is pin 2 and RIGHT_IR is pin 3.

9
00:00:28,614 --> 00:00:32,245
ON_LINE says which value means black.

10
00:00:32,295 --> 00:00:35,030
For many sensors it is HIGH.

11
00:00:36,350 --> 00:00:39,971
digitalRead reads a pin and gives HIGH or LOW.

12
00:00:40,021 --> 00:00:43,562
Then we print BLACK or WHITE for each sensor.

13
00:00:43,612 --> 00:00:48,270
The short delay slows the printing down so you can read it.

14
00:00:49,650 --> 00:00:54,650
Upload the sketch and open the Serial Monitor at 9600 baud.

15
00:00:54,700 --> 00:00:57,989
Slide the robot slowly across the line.

16
00:00:58,039 --> 00:01:03,210
You should see the left sensor say BLACK, then the right one.

17
00:01:04,550 --> 00:01:09,406
If black shows as WHITE, your module is the other way round:

18
00:01:09,456 --> 00:01:11,205
change ON_LINE to LOW.

19
00:01:11,255 --> 00:01:14,721
If a sensor never changes, adjust its knob.

20
00:01:14,771 --> 00:01:17,910
If nothing prints, check the baud rate.

21
00:01:19,400 --> 00:01:20,623
Let us recap.

22
00:01:20,673 --> 00:01:23,755
digitalRead() gives HIGH or LOW.

23
00:01:23,805 --> 00:01:28,160
The Serial Monitor shows what the robot sees.

24
00:01:28,210 --> 00:01:31,488
Set ON_LINE to match your sensors.

25
00:01:31,538 --> 00:01:35,110
Next: Controlling the motors in code.
